#  medical decision-support system predicts whether a patient has a disease or not, with 
probabilities P=[0.9,0.1]. Another patient's predicted probabilities are Q=[0.5,0.5]. 
Write a Python program to calculate the entropy of both predictions and to compare their 
entropy values in a bar chart. Identify which prediction has greater uncertainty. 





import numpy as np
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

P = np.array([0.9,0.1])
Q = np.array([0.5,0.5])

H1 = -np.sum(P*np.log2(P))
H2 = -np.sum(Q*np.log2(Q))
print("P entropy:", H1)
print("Q entropy:", H2)
plt.bar(["P","Q"],[H1,H2])
plt.show()
